/-!
# Displacement of the whole moving G₂ radius

The actual critical actor image has order eight. The natural pointwise-fixer
calculation puts the commutator of V_a intersect Q_c with the opposite seed
inside the original critical commutator, hence inside Z_a.

In the fixed-derived branch, [V_a,V_a] lies in every incident edge radius:
residual fixation makes [V_a,V_t] normal in the whole vertex stabilizer, and
the conjugate edge radii generate V_a. Thus the derived subgroup lies in Q_c.
Involution generation makes the whole radius image there elementary, and the
actual G₂ two-rank bounds its order by eight. This gives the projected-offender
inequality on the literal quotient Vcirc_a/Z(Vcirc_a).

That quotient is generated by residual commutators. Its separating invariant
commutator forms also show that it has no residual fixed vectors. These are
inputs for recognizing the whole quotient; natural recognition and exclusion
of the nonfixed derived-radius branch remain with
qt-e-ms-small-g2-reconstruction. The original SmallMSPair has no fixed-derived
hypothesis. Neither the FF conclusion nor the numerical bound alone is the
required natural model.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher, *Pushing up weak BN-pairs of rank two*,
(3.8), printed pp.878--879; Aschbacher--Smith C.1.31--32, pp.135--136.
The private image-cardinality identity is reused via `import all`; no private
name occurs in a public statement. The octonion model uses the attributed
ATLAS port; see LICENSES/ATLAS.txt.
-/

public noncomputable section
